/**
 * Mark this transaction as aborted.
 *
 * @remarks
 *
 * **SQL equivalent**: `ROLLBACK;` — discards all writes performed inside the transaction.
 *
 * For write transactions (inside {@link LmdbEnv.transaction}): the wrapper callback detects this flag and throws an internal abort error, causing LMDB to roll back all writes in the transaction.
 *
 * For read transactions: releases the underlying LMDB read transaction immediately. Safe to call multiple times.
 *
 * Inside {@link LmdbEnv.transactionFast} this **throws** `LmdbError`: that path commits through lmdb-js `db.transaction()`, which cannot roll back. Silently ignoring the call would let the caller believe the writes were discarded when they are in fact committed.
 *
 * @example
 * ```typescript
 * await env.transaction(async (tx) => {
 *   try {
 *     await users.put("u1", user, tx);
 *     await someRiskyOp();
 *     tx.commit();
 *   } catch (err) {
 *     tx.abort();
 *     throw err;
 *   }
 * });
 * ```
 *
 * @public
 */
